elf ISO certified for this and only adheres to recognised ISO standards.","risk":"Data security and cyber risk"},{"note":"As part of the flavours and fragrances industry the Company must comply with evolving environmental, social and governance regulations amid rising sustainability expectations; mitigated through a phased ESG roadmap with defined actions across sites, energy-efficient systems, environmental infrastructure and EPR registration.","risk":"ESG compliance risk"},{"note":"Operating across multiple geographies exposes the Company to varying economic conditions and market dynamics, and concentration of revenues in specific geographies may increase the sensitivity of earnings to regional volatility; mitigated through a calibrated expansion strategy to keep a well-diversified geographic revenue mix and a comprehensive disaster recovery framework.","risk":"Geographical business risk / revenue concentration by region"},{"note":"The industry's attractive growth potential continues to draw both domestic and global players, heightening competitive intensity that may influence pricing and earnings; mitigated by brand equity, long-standing customer relationships, a diversified product portfolio, innovation and a disciplined operating approach with a healthy balance sheet.","risk":"Competition risk"},{"note":"Management states the Company reported its performance despite significant challenges arising from geopolitical uncertainty, which weighed on the ingredients/export-facing business and on global operating conditions.","risk":"Geopolitical uncertainty affecting demand and operations"},{"note":"The Secretarial Audit Report for FY 2025-26 carries a remark that intimation of a cautionary notice received from NSE on 01 April 2025 was submitted to the stock exchanges on 03 April 2025, beyond the 24-hour timeline prescribed under Regulation 30 of the Listing Regulations; the Board clarified the then-Compliance Officer became aware only on 03 April 2025 and filed the s